 "_comment": "Flux 2 dev with native reference-image conditioning, flattened from ComfyUI 0.37s shipped image_flux2_fp8 template with scripts/ui2api.py. Two reference pictures are VAE-encoded and chained through ReferenceLatent, which is how Flux 2 carries an identity into a new scene without a trained LoRA. Node 42 is reference one AND decides the output size (GetImageSize reads it), node 46 is reference two. sg1_95 true = 8-step turbo LoRA, false = 20 steps.",
 "_notes": [
  "42.inputs.image is the identity reference and sets the canvas: give it the hero portrait at the aspect you want out.",
  "sg1_6.inputs.text is the prompt; sg1_25.inputs.noise_seed the seed; 9.inputs.filename_prefix the output.",
  "sg1_95.inputs.value = true picks the 8-step turbo path (sg1_92), false the 20-step one (sg1_90).",
  "there is no negative prompt on this graph - Flux 2 uses BasicGuider, like the H3 and LTX distilled graphs."
 ]
